# The Water Crystal: "{4}{U}{U}, {T}: Each opponent mills cards equal to the number of cards in your hand." (CR 701.17a)
# Turn 1: the Crystal, then Mox Emerald pays for Sol Ring, and Bot1's hand is empty. Turn 3: Bot1 plays the Island it drew
# and activates with no card in hand: Bot2 mills zero. Zero is not "one or more", so the Crystal's replacement adds nothing.
# Turn 5: Bot1 holds the Counterspell it drew and activates again with one card in hand. Bot2 mills one, plus four from
# the Crystal: five. Bot2's own, larger hand does not count. Both activations use exactly the six mana tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
The Water Crystal
Mox Emerald
Sol Ring
Island
Counterspell
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

